   "summary": "Nearly all of these commenters oppose the proposed census rule and ask the Bureau to withdraw it. They argue that the Constitution and the 14th Amendment require counting all residents regardless of immigration status, and that excluding people would distort apportionment and federal funding. Others object to the winter-residence approach for snowbirds, saying it would shift seats and money away from colder states, and to dropping race and ethnicity questions, which they say are needed for civil rights enforcement, health planning, and community visibility. A few ask for a longer comment period. One commenter supports the rule, saying noncitizens should not count toward apportionment and that a citizenship question should be added.",
