   "check_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
   "summary": "Every comment in this sample opposes the proposed streamlined permitting for oil and gas production sites in the National Petroleum Reserve in Alaska. Most use a shared template that calls the plan a shortcut and asks for full, project-specific environmental review under NEPA, including cumulative impacts, along with continued public input and Tribal consultation. A second template focuses on bird habitat, especially the Teshekpuk Lake Special Area, and on caribou, whales, polar bears and Indigenous communities. Both groups raise concerns about wildlife, wetlands, subsistence resources and climate change in a rapidly warming Arctic.",
