   "summary": "Every comment in this sample opposes the proposed rule and asks the Department of Labor to withdraw or reconsider it. The central objection is that the rule would turn silence into consent by making electronic delivery the default, so people would have to opt out to keep paper copies of HIPAA, COBRA and benefit documents. Commenters say seniors, rural residents, low-income households, people with disabilities, military members and the cybersecurity-wary would be hit hardest. They also argue that the rule is driven by insurer savings rather than consumer benefit, that no evidence shows people read and understand electronic notices as well as paper, and that people who want electronic delivery can already opt in.",
